## Context
Prose review panel 2026-06-11 (pre-arXiv): two reviewers reached major-revision
on claim strength, convergent on three findings. These are author-judgment
rewrites of abstract and conclusion — not mechanical.

1. **Headline claim outruns evidence.** "The binding constraint is the data,
   not the model" rests on the unregistered exploratory documents condition,
   N=4 agents, single-query only — and the paper itself notes multi-turn does
   not equalise (Anthropic 0.61→0.38). Reframe as hypothesis; carry k/n
   directional hedging into abstract and conclusion.
2. **ρ=0.92 in the abstract without the across-model-confound caveat.** The
   honest within-model signal is the modest stratified τ; only 3/14 models
   contribute to the binary gap. Abstract must carry the "pooled, in-sample
   existence proof" qualification.
3. **"Falls short of the four-dimensional quality bar" with two dimensions
   measured.** Coherence/provenance/temporality rubric deferred to Phase C;
   scope the claim to measured dimensions.

Suggestion from same review: abstract ~400 words, omits best number
(fusion F1=0.813); consider adding the seeding-mechanism clause and trimming.

## Relevant files
- `slides/manuscript/main.md` — abstract, conclusion, §Exp2 hedging language

## Test
- Re-run prose review panel post-rewrite: methods + adversarial reviewers no
  longer major on claim strength.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Headline data-vs-model claim reframed as hypothesis with explicit scope.
- [ ] ρ=0.92 carries the pooled/confound caveat wherever it appears.
- [ ] Quality-bar claim scoped to the two measured dimensions.
- [ ] Author has read and blessed the rewritten abstract + conclusion.
